  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sulaiman P vs State Of Kerala on 27 February, 2025",
    "facts": "2. The specific allegation in the complaint filed by the 2 nd respondent Food Safety Officer is that, at about 12.50 p.m on 12.2.2021, he inspected the premises of the food business establishment 'M/s Salmanya Supermarket' and collected the sample 'Nandini Goodlife Toned Milk'. Later, on analysis, the sample was found to contain 'Aflatoxin M1' to an extent of not less than 0.654 micrograms/kg, which is above the prescribed limit as per Regulation 2.2.1 of the Food Safety and Standards (Contaminants, Toxins and Residues) Regulations, 2011. The petitioner being the licencee of the Supermarket is arrayed as the 2025:KER:16587 2nd accused, the manufacturer as the 7 th accused and the 5th accused being the person who marketed the products.",
